      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Predicted high-risk share vs this model's baseline",
      "description": "The dashed line is credit_baseline_high_risk_share, published by the API at model load from registry metadata — what this model flagged on its evaluation set. A live share that wanders 10 points off it means the scored population is no longer the population the model was fitted on, or the threshold moved silently. Deliberately not the 22.12% label prevalence: that is how many accounts default, not how many the model flags, and the two coincide only for a near-perfect classifier.",
