    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Reading the Population Stability Index",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 21
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "PSI compares the distribution of a feature in recent traffic against the distribution captured when the model was trained:\n\n`PSI = Σ (actual − expected) · ln(actual / expected)` over 10 quantile bins.\n\n| PSI | Reading | Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| `< 0.10` | stable | none |\n| `0.10 – 0.25` | moderate shift | review at the next model review |\n| `> 0.25` | significant shift | investigate; the training distribution is gone |\n\nDrift does **not** trigger a retrain automatically. That is a deliberate design decision: the alert notifies a human, the human decides, and the Airflow pipeline is re-run against fresh batches. An automatic retrain loop makes the system respond to its own metrics with nobody accountable for the decision, and it is the first thing to break unattended."
      },
      "transparent": false
    },
